# RUNBOOK-001 — SOC Shift Start

**Status:** Active 
**Runbook ID:** RUNBOOK-001 
**Associated Dashboard:** SOC-OPS-001 
**Platform:** Splunk Enterprise 
**Environment:** corp.lab

---

## Purpose

RUNBOOK-001 defines the standard analyst workflow for beginning a SOC monitoring shift.

The objective is to establish environment health before beginning normal security monitoring.

An analyst should determine:

```text
Are monitored systems reporting?

Is important security telemetry available?

Is there authentication activity requiring review?

Is unusual remote access occurring?

Is PowerShell activity elevated?

Have privileged groups changed?

Are there detection-relevant events requiring investigation?
```

---

# Workflow

```text
Start Analyst Shift
       |
       v
Open SOC-OPS-001
       |
       v
Validate Reporting Hosts
       |
       v
Review Telemetry Status
       |
       v
Review Detection Telemetry Health
       |
       v
Review Authentication Activity
       |
       v
Review Remote Network Logons
       |
       v
Review PowerShell Activity
       |
       v
Review Privileged Changes
       |
       v
Review Detection-Relevant Activity
