---

# Step 1 — Open SOC-OPS-001

Open:

```text
SOC Operations & Detection Health
```

Default review period:

```text
Last 24 Hours
```

A shorter timeframe may be used when investigating recent activity.

---

# Step 2 — Validate Reporting Hosts

Review:

```text
Telemetry Health — Reporting Hosts
```

Confirm expected active systems are represented.

Expected systems depend on which lab VMs are currently powered on.

### Investigate If

- An expected powered-on endpoint is absent
- A host has unexpectedly stopped reporting
- Event volume is significantly different from normal lab activity

---

# Step 3 — Review Telemetry Status

Review:

```text
Telemetry Status
```

Status definitions:

| Status | Definition |
|---|---|
| HEALTHY | Last event ≤ 5 minutes |
| DELAYED | Last event 5–15 minutes |
| STALE | Last event > 15 minutes |

### HEALTHY

No telemetry-health action required.

### DELAYED

Verify whether the endpoint is:

- Powered on
- Network connected
- Actively generating telemetry

Continue monitoring.

### STALE

Determine whether the host is expected to be active.

If active, investigate the telemetry path.

---

# Step 4 — Review Detection Telemetry Health

Open:

```text
Detection Telemetry Health
```

Review the last observed timestamps for:

```text
4624 — Windows Logon
4625 — Failed Authentication
4104 — PowerShell
4698 — Scheduled Task
4728 — Group Membership Change
```

Do not automatically classify an absent event type as a sensor failure.

Some telemetry is activity-dependent.

---

# Step 5 — Review Failed Authentication

Open:

```text
Failed Authentication by Account
```

Look for:

- Repeated failures
- Administrative accounts
- Unexpected usernames
- Sudden increases
- Accounts with failures followed by successful authentication

### Potential Follow-Up

Pivot into:

```spl
index=* (EventCode=4624 OR EventCode=4625)
| sort _time
| table _time host EventCode TargetUserName IpAddress LogonType
```

---

# Step 6 — Review Remote Network Authentication

Open:

```text
Remote Network Logons
```

Review:

```text
TargetUserName
IpAddress
Network-logon volume
```

Look for:

- Unexpected source IP addresses
- Administrative account usage
- New source/account combinations
- One source accessing multiple endpoints
- Activity inconsistent with expected administration

---

# Step 7 — Review PowerShell Activity

Review:

```text
PowerShell Activity by Host
```

and:

```text
PowerShell Activity Timeline
```

Look for:

- Unexpected hosts
- Sudden activity spikes
- PowerShell activity following remote authentication
- Activity associated with an existing investigation

PowerShell execution itself does not establish malicious activity.

---

# Step 8 — Review Privileged Group Changes

Review:

```text
Recent Privileged Group Changes
```

and:

```text
Domain Admin Membership Changes
```

Determine:

```text
Who performed the change?
Which account was added?
Which group was modified?
Was the change expected?
Was the activity authorized?
```

Unexpected privileged-group modification should receive immediate analyst review.

---

# Step 9 — Review Detection-Relevant Activity

Open:

```text
Detection-Relevant Event Activity
```

This panel provides visibility into underlying events associated with detection logic.

It does not represent actual alert-trigger counts.

Review unusually high or unexpected activity associated with:

```text
DET-002
DET-003
DET-004
DET-005
DET-006
```

---

# Step 10 — Review Host Activity

Review:

```text
Security Events by Host
```

and:

```text
Telemetry Coverage by Host
```

Look for:

- Unexpectedly active endpoints
- Significant differences between hosts
- Hosts generating unusually limited telemetry
- Sudden changes in event diversity

---

# Step 11 — Review MITRE ATT&CK Coverage

Review:

```text
MITRE ATT&CK Coverage
```

This panel is primarily an analytic inventory rather than a live threat indicator.

Use it to understand which ATT&CK behaviors are represented by the current detection portfolio.

---

