# Telemetry Troubleshooting Workflow

If an expected active host is stale:

```text
Host Appears STALE
       |
       v
Confirm VM / Host Is Running
       |
       v
Confirm Network Connectivity
       |
       v
Confirm Domain Connectivity
       |
       v
Check Splunk Forwarder
       |
       v
Check Local Windows Events
       |
       v
Compare Local Event Time
With Splunk Last-Seen Time
       |
       v
Identify Ingestion Delay
or Collection Failure
```

---

# Domain Connectivity Check

For domain-joined workstations:

```powershell
Test-ComputerSecureChannel -Verbose
```

Expected:

```text
True
```

A broken domain secure channel should be treated as an infrastructure issue unless additional evidence indicates security relevance.

---

# Splunk Forwarder Check

On the affected Windows endpoint:

```powershell
Get-Service SplunkForwarder
```

Expected:

```text
Running
```

If the endpoint has local events but Splunk is not receiving them, investigate the forwarding path.

---

# Analyst Decision Matrix

| Observation | Initial Action |
|---|---|
| Expected host absent | Validate host and forwarder |
| Host telemetry stale | Investigate ingestion |
| Multiple failed logons | Review account/source |
| Unexpected network logon | Investigate remote source |
| PowerShell spike | Review scripts/activity |
| Remote logon followed by PowerShell | Review CORR-002 context |
| Unexpected privileged change | Immediate investigation |
| Missing activity-dependent EventCode | Verify before treating as failure |

---

# Escalation Criteria

Activity should receive additional investigation when one or more of the following are observed:

- Unexpected administrative account activity
- Repeated authentication failures
- Successful authentication following suspicious failures
- Remote authentication from an unexpected source
- Remote authentication followed by PowerShell
- Unexpected privileged group modification
- Suspicious PowerShell behavior
- Multiple related detection behaviors
- Unexplained telemetry loss from an active endpoint

---

# Shift-Start Completion Criteria

The shift-start review is complete when the analyst has:

```text
[ ] Reviewed reporting hosts
[ ] Reviewed telemetry freshness
[ ] Reviewed detection telemetry health
[ ] Reviewed failed authentication
[ ] Reviewed remote network authentication
[ ] Reviewed PowerShell activity
[ ] Reviewed privileged group changes
[ ] Reviewed detection-relevant activity
[ ] Reviewed endpoint activity
[ ] Identified or cleared anomalies
```

---

# Operational Principle

Telemetry health must be established before relying on detection results.

```text
No Alert
```

does not necessarily mean:

```text
No Malicious Activity
```

if the telemetry required by the detection is unavailable.

Therefore:

```text
Telemetry Health
       |
       v
Detection Confidence
       |
       v
Analyst Decision
```

